    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full `mvn test` build passes green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe create audit line now also logs `membershipLevel` (already present) and the newly added `membershipNumber`, while keeping every previously logged field.\n\nTo avoid duplicating the membership-number formatting rule, I extracted it into a new util class that matches the existing pattern of `MembershipLevel`/`MembershipPoints`:\n\n- **`util/MembershipNumber.java`** (new) \u2014 single-responsibility helper holding the `<customerCode>-M<YY>` formatting (with the same null-guards the mapper had).\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `membershipNumber(owner)` now delegates to `MembershipNumber.of(owner)` instead of inlining the format, so the response DTO and the audit line share one source of truth.\n- **`rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 the `AUDIT.info(...)` call gained a `membershipNumber={}` field populated via `MembershipNumber.of(owner)`.\n\nThe acceptance test \u2014 which asserts the audit line contains both the response's `membershipNumber` and `membershipLevel` \u2014 passes, and `mvn test` is green.",
